# Arkanoid / Breakout

Vanilla browser Breakout clone. No package.json, bundler, framework, or tests.

Playable shell at repo root: `index.html`, `style.css`, `game.js`, `levels.js`, `powerups.js`.
Atlas + audio under `assets/`. Specs under `specs/` (01 MVP, 02 explosions, 03 levels/pause, 04 power-ups and level speed).

## Tech Stack
- HTML5 + JavaScript ES6+ + Canvas 2D
- Sprite atlas via `assets/spritesheet.js` (globals: `loadSpritesheet`, `drawSprite`, `drawFrame`, `SPRITES`, `EXPLOSION_FRAMES`, `EXPLOSION_DURATION`)
- Audio: `HTMLAudioElement` / `Audio` (mp3)
- Zero npm/runtime deps
- Global scripts, no ES modules. Order in `index.html`: `assets/spritesheet.js`, `levels.js`, `powerups.js`, `game.js`

## Commands
```bash
python3 -m http.server 8000
# or: npx serve .
# then open http://localhost:8000 (or 3000)
```
No build, test, or lint scripts. Static server required (Image/Audio from `file://` can fail).

## Project Layout
```
/
  index.html
  style.css
  game.js                   # loop, paddle, balls, bricks, serve, levelBallSpeed
  levels.js                 # COLS, ROWS, ROW_COLORS, LEVELS
  powerups.js               # drops, effects, shots, POWER HUD helpers
  README.md
  skills-lock.json
  specs/
    .spec-config.yml
    01-mvp-arkanoid.md
    02-block-breaking-animation.md
    03-levels-pause-change.md
    04-powerups-and-level-speed.md
  assets/
    spritesheet.js          # atlas API (do not rewrite coords)
    spritesheet-breakout.png
    sounds/
      ball-bounce.mp3
      break-sound.mp3
    __MACOSX/               # junk from zip extract; ignore
```

`spritesheet.js` loads `assets/spritesheet-breakout.png` relative to the page URL (repo root). Sounds: `assets/sounds/*.mp3`.

## Code Standards
- Match `spritesheet.js`: 2-space indent, single quotes, `const`/`let` (no `var`), spaces inside parens (`function foo( cb )`).
- Draw paddle, ball, bricks via atlas helpers; do not hardcode `sx/sy/sw/sh` outside `spritesheet.js`.
- Sprite names for `drawSprite`: `paddle`, `ball`, `block_<color>`.
- Block/explosion colors: `gray`, `red`, `yellow`, `cyan`, `magenta`, `hotpink`, `green`. Gray unused in current patterns.
- Explosions: `EXPLOSION_FRAMES[color]` (4 frames), duration `EXPLOSION_DURATION` (150ms).
- Capsules and laser shots are canvas fills, not atlas sprites.
- Prefer a `requestAnimationFrame` loop with `update(dt)` + `draw()` in `game.js`.
- `levels.js` owns `COLS`, `ROWS`, `ROW_COLORS`, `LEVELS` (five 13x6 ASCII grids). Do not redeclare them in `game.js`.
- `powerups.js` owns drop/catch/tick/draw/clear/remap helpers, `breaksInLevel`, `powerups`, `shots`, `effects`. Do not redeclare them in `game.js`.
- `game.js` keeps the loop, bricks, paddle, `balls` array, `levelBallSpeed` / `currentBallSpeed`, serve, and paddle bounce. Helpers in `powerups.js` read those globals at call time.
- HUD: SCORE, LEVEL, POWER (`#power`), LIVES. POWER tokens in order `W S T M L` (skip `E`). Inactive `--`.
- Balls are an array (cap 3). Lose a life only when `balls.length === 0`.
- Ball speed: `BALL_SPEED * SCALE * (1.15 ** (level - 1))`. Slow is `* 0.7` of that, every live ball.
- Power-up types: `wide`, `slow`, `life`, `sticky`, `multi`, `laser`. Capsule letters W cyan, S yellow, E green, T magenta, M red, L gray.
- Draw order: bricks, explosions, capsules, paddle, balls, shots.
- Pause (P) freezes motion and timers. `clearPowerups` on loadLevel, new game, life miss, Win, Lose.

## Constraints
- NEVER add frameworks (Phaser, Pixi, React), bundlers, TypeScript, or npm deps unless explicitly requested.
- NEVER edit atlas coordinates or invent sprite names/colors not in `SPRITES` / `EXPLOSION_FRAMES`.
- NEVER treat `__MACOSX/`, `.DS_Store`, or `*:Zone.Identifier` as source.
- Keep classic Breakout: paddle, balls, brick grid, wall bounce, lose life on bottom miss, clear bricks to win.
- Audio files: only `ball-bounce.mp3` and `break-sound.mp3` unless new assets are added.
- ASCII-only in `.md` files (no tildes/accents). Do not invent a test/lint toolchain unless asked.
- Do not add a seventh power-up, extra life above 3, auto-fire, more than one shot, or more than 3 balls unless a spec says so.
